1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,825
A potato that grows long
and thin, like a spindle.

2
00:00:03,825 --> 00:00:06,290
A cow that stumbles and cannot stand.

3
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:09,469
A virus, the smallest
germ we have met so far.

4
00:00:09,869 --> 00:00:11,481
The first two are sick.

5
00:00:11,481 --> 00:00:13,491
But the cause is not a virus.

6
00:00:13,491 --> 00:00:15,387
It is something even simpler.

7
00:00:15,837 --> 00:00:18,364
Diya read this in her notes and stopped.

8
00:00:18,364 --> 00:00:22,705
Something with no protein coat, or
with no genes at all, can still cause

9
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:23,605
disease?

10
00:00:23,712 --> 00:00:28,244
By the end, you will know two such
agents, viroids and prions, and how

11
00:00:28,244 --> 00:00:30,380
to tell them apart from viruses.

12
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,574
First, let's remember what a virus is.

13
00:00:33,924 --> 00:00:40,202
A virus is nucleic acid, RNA or DNA,
inside a protein coat called the capsid.

14
00:00:40,652 --> 00:00:43,657
Now imagine an agent with RNA but no coat.

15
00:00:43,657 --> 00:00:45,051
That is a viroid.

16
00:00:45,051 --> 00:00:48,805
And one with no nucleic
acid at all, only a protein.

17
00:00:48,805 --> 00:00:50,146
That is a prion.

18
00:00:50,796 --> 00:00:52,576
Let's start with the viroid.

19
00:00:52,576 --> 00:00:55,912
Zoom into a sick potato
plant, one level at a time.

20
00:00:56,262 --> 00:00:59,873
The plant looks weak, and its
tubers grow long and thin.

21
00:00:59,873 --> 00:01:02,205
This is potato spindle tuber disease.

22
00:01:02,705 --> 00:01:03,605
Zoom in.

23
00:01:03,435 --> 00:01:07,576
A potato tuber, the part we eat,
stretched into a spindle shape.

24
00:01:08,076 --> 00:01:09,117
Zoom again.

25
00:01:09,117 --> 00:01:12,792
Inside one cell, there
is no virus to be seen.

26
00:01:12,792 --> 00:01:14,772
Only tiny pieces of RNA.

27
00:01:15,272 --> 00:01:16,860
Zoom into one piece.

28
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:20,592
This is a viroid: free
RNA, with no protein coat.

29
00:01:20,592 --> 00:01:25,262
Its RNA is of low molecular weight,
which means it is very small.

30
00:01:25,912 --> 00:01:26,930
Who found it?

31
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:32,189
In nineteen seventy one, TO Diener
discovered a new infectious agent,

32
00:01:32,189 --> 00:01:36,626
smaller than viruses, that caused
potato spindle tuber disease.

33
00:01:37,076 --> 00:01:39,211
It was found to be a free RNA.

34
00:01:39,211 --> 00:01:42,015
It lacked the protein
coat found in viruses.

35
00:01:42,015 --> 00:01:43,796
So it was named a viroid.

36
00:01:44,446 --> 00:01:45,538
Now the prion.

37
00:01:45,538 --> 00:01:48,969
To understand it, we need
to know how proteins work.

38
00:01:48,969 --> 00:01:50,013
Step by step.

39
00:01:50,363 --> 00:01:51,263
Step one.

40
00:01:51,249 --> 00:01:55,378
A protein is a long chain that
folds into an exact shape.

41
00:01:55,378 --> 00:01:57,378
Its shape decides its job.

42
00:01:58,128 --> 00:01:59,028
Step two.

43
00:01:58,981 --> 00:02:02,580
A prion is a protein that
has folded the wrong way.

44
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,598
An abnormally folded protein.

45
00:02:05,348 --> 00:02:06,265
Step three.

46
00:02:06,265 --> 00:02:10,846
When a prion meets a normal protein
of the same kind, it makes that one

47
00:02:10,846 --> 00:02:12,121
fold wrongly too.

48
00:02:12,871 --> 00:02:13,771
Step four.

49
00:02:13,689 --> 00:02:16,830
Now there are two prions,
then four, then many.

50
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:18,429
It is a chain reaction.

51
00:02:19,179 --> 00:02:20,111
Step five.

52
00:02:20,111 --> 00:02:24,457
The wrongly folded proteins pile
up and damage the nerve cells.

53
00:02:24,457 --> 00:02:28,140
So prion diseases are diseases
of the nervous system.

54
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:31,074
Which diseases do prions cause?

55
00:02:31,424 --> 00:02:36,916
In cattle, bovine spongiform
encephalopathy, or BSE, commonly called mad

56
00:02:36,916 --> 00:02:38,087
cow disease.

57
00:02:38,537 --> 00:02:40,170
Bovine means of cattle.

58
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:42,262
Spongiform means like a sponge.

59
00:02:42,262 --> 00:02:45,120
Encephalopathy means a
disease of the brain.

60
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:48,347
The brain becomes full
of holes, like a sponge.

61
00:02:48,797 --> 00:02:52,573
In humans, a similar prion
disease is called CJD.

62
00:02:52,573 --> 00:02:56,065
And prions are about the
same size as viruses.

63
00:02:56,715 --> 00:02:59,167
Now let's put all three side by side.

64
00:02:59,517 --> 00:03:02,780
A virus has nucleic
acid and a protein coat.

65
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,345
Example: the tobacco mosaic virus.

66
00:03:05,795 --> 00:03:10,541
A viroid has only free RNA, of
low molecular weight, and no coat.

67
00:03:10,541 --> 00:03:13,465
Example: the potato spindle tuber viroid.

68
00:03:13,915 --> 00:03:17,014
A prion has only protein, wrongly folded.

69
00:03:17,014 --> 00:03:19,949
Example: the agent of mad cow disease.

70
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:21,630
Your turn.

71
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:24,866
An agent has RNA, but no protein coat.

72
00:03:24,866 --> 00:03:26,324
Virus or viroid?

73
00:03:26,324 --> 00:03:27,842
Pause and decide.

74
00:03:31,042 --> 00:03:31,942
Viroid!

75
00:03:31,798 --> 00:03:34,516
A virus always has a protein coat.

76
00:03:34,516 --> 00:03:36,350
A viroid is free RNA.

77
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,202
Remember this.

78
00:03:38,202 --> 00:03:40,337
Viroid: RNA with no coat.

79
00:03:40,337 --> 00:03:42,864
Prion: a wrongly folded protein.

80
00:03:43,464 --> 00:03:44,993
Now a worked example.

81
00:03:44,993 --> 00:03:47,703
Let's sort four agents with a simple key.

82
00:03:48,053 --> 00:03:50,821
Question one: does it have nucleic acid?

83
00:03:50,821 --> 00:03:52,629
If not, it is a prion.

84
00:03:52,629 --> 00:03:54,687
The BSE agent drops out here.

85
00:03:55,137 --> 00:03:57,983
Question two: does it have a protein coat?

86
00:03:57,983 --> 00:03:59,790
If not, it is a viroid.

87
00:03:59,790 --> 00:04:02,480
The potato spindle tuber agent stops here.

88
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:05,398
If it has both, it is a virus.

89
00:04:05,398 --> 00:04:09,582
The tobacco mosaic virus and the
bacteriophage both land here.

90
00:04:10,232 --> 00:04:11,697
Now, the exam trap.

91
00:04:12,047 --> 00:04:16,376
Many students write that viroid
RNA is of high molecular weight.

92
00:04:16,776 --> 00:04:18,568
But it is the opposite.

93
00:04:18,568 --> 00:04:23,238
Viroid RNA is of low molecular
weight, and it has no protein coat.

94
00:04:23,238 --> 00:04:26,379
That is why viroids are
smaller than viruses.

95
00:04:27,029 --> 00:04:28,553
Where is this asked?

96
00:04:28,553 --> 00:04:33,082
NEET has asked it as a statement
question: which line about viroids is

97
00:04:33,082 --> 00:04:36,017
wrong, or how viroids differ from viruses.

98
00:04:36,617 --> 00:04:37,834
Exam level now.

99
00:04:37,834 --> 00:04:39,629
Read the four statements.

100
00:04:39,629 --> 00:04:41,320
Which ones are correct?

101
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,589
Pause and solve.

102
00:04:47,989 --> 00:04:49,300
The answer is A.

103
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,068
Statements one and three.

104
00:04:51,568 --> 00:04:52,768
Two is wrong.

105
00:04:52,768 --> 00:04:55,913
Viroids are free RNA with no protein coat.

106
00:04:56,413 --> 00:04:57,565
Four is wrong.

107
00:04:57,565 --> 00:05:01,196
Mad cow disease is caused
by a prion, not a viroid.

108
00:05:01,796 --> 00:05:03,255
Here is your recap.

109
00:05:03,255 --> 00:05:04,755
Screenshot this card.

110
00:05:07,955 --> 00:05:10,953
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

111
00:05:11,353 --> 00:05:12,253
One.

112
00:05:11,858 --> 00:05:14,670
What does a viroid lack that a virus has?

113
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:16,470
Two.

114
00:05:16,083 --> 00:05:17,903
What is a prion made of?

115
00:05:18,803 --> 00:05:19,703
Three.

116
00:05:19,445 --> 00:05:22,859
What does the word spongiform
tell you about BSE?

117
00:05:23,959 --> 00:05:27,683
Next time: curd, idli
batter and a compost pit.

118
00:05:27,683 --> 00:05:30,661
Which tiny workers are behind all three?

119
00:05:30,661 --> 00:05:35,401
We find out in economic and ecological
importance of microorganisms.
